
ROTINC
++++++

SUMMARY
-------

Rotate a set of 3 perpendicular seismograms

SYNTAX
------

  ``ROTINC TO [VRT|LQT|VNE|XYZ] { INCIDENCE i | iP | iS } { VP alpha VS beta RAY{DEG|KM} par {FREESURFACE} } ``

INPUT
-----
      :TO VRT: rotate into vertical,radial, transverse coordinate system

      :TO LQT: rotate into P,SV, and SH coordinate system

      :TO VNE: rotate into system aligned with N, E and vertical

      :TO XYZ: rotate into system aligned with N, E and vertical
          Z: Up, X: East, Y: North

      :INCIDENCE iP: Use P wave to determine angle of L direction

      :INCIDENCE iS: Use S wave to determine angle of L direction

      :INCIDENCE i: Define angle from vertical of L direction

      :VP v: P wave velocity near surface (default 5.8)

      :VS v: S wave velocity near surface (default 3.35)

      :RAYDEG v: ray parameter = horizontal slowness (s/deg)

      :RAYKM v: ray parameter= horizontal slowness (s/km)

      :FREESURFACE: use free surface response instead of propagation vector

DEFAULT VALUES
--------------

 None

DESCRIPTION
-----------

  Given three perpendicular components of the same seismogram, rotate the set
  into coordinate systems. It works its way through all records in memory
  until it fails to find 3 consecutive perpendicular traces. It assumes
  vertical up (cmpinc = 0.0), cmpaz measured clockwise from N.

HEADER CHANGES
--------------

  CMPINC, CMPAZ, KCMPNM, DEPMAX, DEPMIN, DEPMEN

ERROR MESSAGES
--------------
- 1002: Bad value for
- 1011: Bad command file syntax
- 1301: No data file read in.
- 1304: Illegal operation on data file
- 1336: Undefined header field value.

